# lost_way — the outcome, not the verb.
#
# A failed walk that loses the way: the chip is shown with the failure, and the CONTINUE that closes
# the segment ends the visit — back on the world map, not in the next area and not in this one.
# --penalty-only get_lost pins the draw, which is otherwise uniform over move's table.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Yard" --penalty-only get_lost

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal move
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE
expect-verb move
expect Lost the way
expect-no-outcome area_move

# --- the outcome really ran ---
expect-outcome lost_way

# --- after: still standing in the place until the press that closes the segment ---
expect-state where Test Field
click button
wait mode WorldView 60
quit
